"I inspected the implementation and ran the shipped verifier.\n\nCommand run:\n- `npm run verify:photoreal` → `Verified bookmark sidecars and immutable photoreal gallery behavior for 4 scripted case groups`\n\nFindings:\n\n1. PASS: Bookmark data is sidecar state, not part of the editable snapshot, and bookmark creation is non-versioning — `packages/contracts/src/scene.ts` defines `Scene` with separate `snapshot`, `bookmarks`, and `photoreal_gallery` fields; `apps/api/src/roomplan-persistence.ts` persists `camera_bookmarks` separately from `scene_snapshot`; `apps/api/src/roomplan-ingest.ts#createBookmark` only appends to `stored.scene.bookmarks` / `persisted_records.camera_bookmarks` and does not change `scene.head.current_scene_version` or `scene.snapshot`; `scripts/verify-photoreal-sidecars.mts` asserts bookmark creation must not increment version or rewrite the head snapshot.\n\n2. PASS: The API contract and server expose `POST /scenes/{scene_id}/photoreal` with immutable snapshot input and job-based output — `packages/contracts/src/api.ts` defines `GeneratePhotorealRequest { scene_snapshot_id, bookmark_id?, camera_pose?, fov?, prompt_modifiers, idempotency_key }` and `GeneratePhotorealResponse { job_id, photoreal_entry }`; `apps/api/src/server.ts` routes `POST .../photoreal` to `context.service.generatePhotoreal(...)`.\n\n3. PASS: Gallery reads are exposed through scene/job reads — `packages/contracts/src/api.ts` defines `SceneReadResponse { scene: Scene }` and `JobReadResponse { job, photoreal_entry? }`; `packages/contracts/src/scene.ts` includes `photoreal_gallery` on `Scene`; `apps/api/src/server.ts` returns `{ scene }` for scene GETs and `{ job, photoreal_entry }` for `GET /jobs/:job_id`; `apps/web/src/server.ts` renders `scene.photoreal_gallery` and displays each entry’s `scene_version`, `scene_snapshot_id`, `bookmark_id`, and `asset_id`.\n\n4. PASS: Photoreal entries are deterministically keyed by scene + immutable version + resolved camera params — `apps/api/src/roomplan-ingest.ts#generatePhotoreal` builds `entrySeed` from `{ scene_id, scene_snapshot_id, scene_version, bookmark_id, camera_pose, fov, prompt_modifiers }`, then derives stable `entry_id` and `asset_id`; `packages/contracts/src/scene.ts` defines `PhotorealEntry` with `scene_version`, `scene_snapshot_id`, `bookmark_id`, `camera_pose`, and `fov`; `apps/api/src/roomplan-persistence.ts` persists them as `PersistedPhotorealEntryRecord extends PhotorealEntry { scene_id }`.\n\n5. PASS: Photoreal generation reuses the same deterministic quick-render conditioning inputs — `apps/api/src/quick-render.ts` builds live quick renders with `buildDeterministicQuickRender(scene, CURATED_ASSET_MANIFEST)`; `apps/api/src/roomplan-ingest.ts#generatePhotoreal` calls that exact same function on `historicalScene`; it stores conditioning metadata in `provider_metadata` (`conditioning_scene_version`, `conditioning_snapshot_id`, asset/surface/object counts). `packages/contracts/src/render.ts` shows `QuickRenderScene` itself is keyed by `scene_id`, `scene_version`, and `scene_snapshot_id`.\n\n6. PASS: Photoreal jobs are tracked, persisted, reloaded, and readable — `packages/contracts/src/api.ts` defines `JobRecord`; `apps/api/src/roomplan-ingest.ts#generatePhotoreal` creates a `JobRecord` with `job_kind: \"photoreal\"`, `status: \"ready\"`, `source_scene_version`, `scene_snapshot_id`, and `output_asset_id`, stores it in `jobsById`, and persists it; the constructor reloads persisted `job_records` via `loadAll()` + `hydrateStoredScene`; `apps/api/src/roomplan-store.ts` includes `job_records?: JobRecord[]`; `apps/api/src/server.ts` exposes `GET /jobs/:job_id` and attaches the matching gallery entry.\n\n7. PASS: Retries with the same idempotency key are idempotent and conflicting reuse is rejected; duplicate immutable-view requests do not duplicate gallery storage — `apps/api/src/roomplan-ingest.ts#getIdempotentResponse` hashes the request body and either returns the recorded response or throws `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`; `generatePhotoreal` checks idempotency before doing work; it only appends to `photoreal_gallery` when no existing `entry_id` matches. `scripts/verify-photoreal-sidecars.mts` asserts: same key returns the same response, gallery length stays `1`, a different request with the same key throws `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`, and a second idempotency key for the same immutable camera+snapshot request reuses the same `entry_id` with gallery length still `1`.\n\n8. PASS: Generating or revisiting older scene versions does not rewrite the current editable head — `apps/api/src/roomplan-ingest.ts#materializeSceneAtSnapshot` returns a cloned scene with only the local `head.current_snapshot_id`, `head.current_scene_version`, `snapshot`, and `derived_state_cache` swapped to the requested snapshot; `generatePhotoreal` uses that cloned `historicalScene` and never assigns it back to `stored.scene`. `scripts/verify-photoreal-sidecars.mts` explicitly asserts historical photoreal generation leaves the current head at version `2` while the returned gallery entry remains pinned to version `1` / the older `scene_snapshot_id`.\n\nAssessment: CONVERGED — implementation matches requirements with no material gaps"
